{"links": {"self": "/works/OL450063W/editions.json?limit=20", "work": "/works/OL450063W", "next": "/works/OL450063W/editions.json?limit=20&offset=20"}, "size": 2185, "entries": [{"works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "title": "Frankenstein", "publishers": ["Points"], "publish_date": "2025", "key": "/books/OL61213652M", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "identifiers": {}, "covers": [15166252], "subtitle": "ou Le Prom\u00e9th\u00e9e moderne", "languages": [{"key": "/languages/fre"}], "translation_of": "Frankenstein", "translated_from": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "physical_format": "Paperback", "number_of_pages": 320, "isbn_13": ["9791041419821"], "latest_revision": 4, "revision": 4, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2026-01-31T23:05:36.197366"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2026-02-04T19:05:00.347364"}}, {"works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "title": "Frankenstein", "publishers": ["Blossom Books"], "publish_date": "April 10, 2019", "key": "/books/OL61200468M", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "identifiers": {}, "covers": [15165840], "isbn_13": ["9789463492515"], "isbn_10": ["9463492518"], "contributors": [{"role": "Editor", "name": "Maria Postema"}, {"role": "Illustrator", "name": "Sophie Pluim"}], "languages": [{"key": "/languages/dut"}], "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "'Er is zo veel geluk om me heen, terwijl ik overal word buitengesloten. Ik was vriendelijk en goed, maar mijn wanhoop heeft me tot slechte daden gedreven.'\r\n\r\nBij Frankenstein denken de meeste mensen aan het grote, groene monster met schroeven in zijn hoofd. Maar dat is niet het verhaal dat Mary Shelley in 1816 opschreef. Dat verhaal gaat over de ambitieuze wetenschapper Victor Frankenstein, die een levend wezen weet te cre\u00ebren. Zijn schepping, het 'monster', voelt zich in de steek gelaten door zijn maker en begint dood en verderf te zaaien \u2013 uit wanhoop.\r\n\r\nMet de Wereldklassiekers hopen we meer jongeren te interesseren in en kennis te laten maken met de klassieke wereldliteratuur. De nieuwe hertalingen blijven dicht op het origineel maar zijn tegelijkertijd zo bewerkt dat ze voor jongeren d\u00e9 opstap vormen naar ander klassiek werk.\r\n\r\nFrankenstein is de tweede klassieker die we aan onze serie toevoegen. Bewerker Maria Postema is dicht bij het origineel gebleven, maar heeft hier en daar ingegrepen om de fijne leesbaarheid te garanderen. Daarnaast heeft Maria uitgebreid research gedaan naar de verschillen in het origineel uit 1818, en de door Shelley bewerkte versie uit 1831. In de nieuwe editie komen beide versies samen."}, "physical_format": "Hardcover", "number_of_pages": 192, "latest_revision": 3, "revision": 3, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2026-01-30T11:01:31.580496"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2026-01-30T11:02:24.694482"}}, {"works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "title": "Frankenstein", "publishers": ["Rakuten Kobo"], "publish_date": "2020", "key": "/books/OL60739655M", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "identifiers": {}, "covers": [15148535], "isbn_13": ["9781774530511"], "publish_places": ["Toronto, Ontario, Canada"], "copyright_date": "2020", "edition_name": "A Kobo Edition", "contributors": [{"role": "Typesetter", "name": "Jessica Khadoo"}, {"role": "Cover Design", "name": "Sam Arnold"}, {"role": "Cover Design", "name": "Solly Bulbulia"}], "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "\u201cI beheld the wretch \u2014 the miserable monster whom I had created. He held up the curtain of the bed; and his eyes, if eyes they may be called, were fixed on me. His jaws opened, and he muttered some inarticulate sounds, while a grin wrinkled his cheeks. He might have spoken, but I did not hear; one hand was stretched out, seemingly to detain me, but I escaped and rushed downstairs.\u201d\r\n\r\nGrieving the sudden death of his mother, young Victor Frankenstein buries himself in his scientific experiments. Along the way he discovers a method to give life to non-living matter, and proves his theory right by creating a grotesque 8-foot tall creature from old body parts and bringing it to life. Horrified by what he has done, Frankenstein abandons his creation and sets off a chain of events that will affect everyone Victor holds dear.\r\n\r\nA twisted tale of reanimation and revenge, Frankenstein explores the minds of both the creator and the creation to find out what it truly means to be human. Considered by many to be the first true science fiction novel, Mary Shelley\u2019s Gothic masterpiece has inspired artists, writers and musicians since its publication in 1818.\r\n\r\nKobo Editions offers this fully-accessible version of the original text for your enjoyment."}, "physical_format": "eBook", "number_of_pages": 242, "latest_revision": 3, "revision": 3, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-12-02T01:29:42.271128"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-12-02T01:34:47.064970"}}, {"publishers": ["Plut\u00f3n Ediciones"], "title": "FRANKENSTEIN. Biling\u00fce", "identifiers": {}, "covers": [8078328], "publish_date": "2013", "key": "/books/OL26385062M", "works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "source_records": ["amazon:8415089457"], "isbn_13": ["9788415089452"], "isbn_10": ["8494639919"], "languages": [{"key": "/languages/spa"}, {"key": "/languages/eng"}], "translation_of": "Frankenstein or The Modern Prometheus", "translated_from": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "Mary Shelley (1797 \u2013 1851) public\u00f3 \u201cFrankenstein\u201d con apenas 20 a\u00f1os de edad. La novela, nacida de una apuesta entre amigos sobre qui\u00e9n escrib\u00eda la mejor historia de terror, narra las vicisitudes de un cient\u00edfico llamado V\u00edctor Frankenstein y el monstruo al que dio vida con sus experimentos. La novela es considerada hoy en d\u00eda como una de las precursoras de la ciencia ficci\u00f3n, y con su est\u00e9tica g\u00f3tica e innegable influencia del romanticismo, sigue cautivado la atenci\u00f3n de lectores alrededor del mundo."}, "physical_format": "Paperback", "number_of_pages": 384, "latest_revision": 4, "revision": 4, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2017-10-09T18:44:05.063235"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-10-29T03:05:37.149804"}}, {"works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "title": "Frankenstein", "publishers": ["Editora Antof\u00e1gica"], "publish_date": "2023", "key": "/books/OL58754411M", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "identifiers": {}, "covers": [14928172], "isbn_13": ["9786580210343"], "contributors": [{"role": "Translator", "name": "F\u00e1bio Bonillo"}], "languages": [{"key": "/languages/por"}], "translation_of": "Frankenstein: or the Modern Prometheus", "translated_from": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "O que forma um ser humano? Neste cl\u00e1ssico de uma das maiores escritoras da hist\u00f3ria, um cientista descobre se basta juntar os \u00f3rg\u00e3os corretos e lhes dar energia vital para criar uma exist\u00eancia humana \u2013 mas n\u00e3o imagina que pode perder completamente o controle. O ambicioso sonho de um cientista est\u00e1 fadado a lev\u00e1-lo a uma jornada de prova\u00e7\u00f5es. Trata-se de Victor Frankenstein, um jovem deslumbrado com a ci\u00eancia e que deseja deixar sua marca nos avan\u00e7os do conhecimento fazendo um experimento in\u00e9dito: a cria\u00e7\u00e3o de um ser humano em laborat\u00f3rio. Publicado originalmente em 1818, este cl\u00e1ssico g\u00f3tico que inaugura a fic\u00e7\u00e3o cient\u00edfica foi escrito por Mary Shelley durante um despretensioso desafio entre amigos e revelou o talento de uma autora que conquistou seu lugar no c\u00e2none mundial. Frankenstein agora recebe uma nova edi\u00e7\u00e3o pela Antof\u00e1gica, traduzida por F\u00e1bio Bonillo, com ilustra\u00e7\u00f5es de Iuri Casaes, al\u00e9m de apresenta\u00e7\u00e3o da crimin\u00f3loga e escritora Ilana Casoy (Bom dia, Ver\u00f4nica) e posf\u00e1cios de Sofia Nestrovski, corroteirista e locutora do podcast \u201cVinte mil l\u00e9guas\u201d, Cristhiano Aguiar, autor de G\u00f3tico nordestino e professor de literatura na Universidade Presbiteriana Mackenzie e Nina da Hora, cientista da computa\u00e7\u00e3o pela PUC-Rio, pesquisadora e ativista brasileira. O QR Code na cinta direciona a duas videoaulas sobre o livro dispon\u00edveis no YouTube com Sofia Nestrovski, escritora e mestre em Teoria Liter\u00e1ria pela USP."}, "physical_format": "Capa Dura", "number_of_pages": 328, "latest_revision": 3, "revision": 3, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-04-28T18:47:24.672581"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-04-28T18:49:55.009426"}}, {"works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "title": "Frankenstein", "publishers": ["RBA Coleccionables, S.A.U."], "publish_date": "2021", "key": "/books/OL57849880M", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "identifiers": {}, "covers": [14845984], "physical_format": "Couverture rigide", "number_of_pages": 290, "isbn_13": ["9788413932699"], "subtitle": "ou le Prom\u00e9th\u00e9e moderne", "languages": [{"key": "/languages/fre"}], "translation_of": "Frankenstein. The 1818 text", "translated_from": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "latest_revision": 4, "revision": 4, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-02-23T14:50:26.953082"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-02-23T14:52:35.577900"}}, {"title": "Frankenstein", "publish_date": "2021", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "languages": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "pagination": "288", "publishers": ["Gallery Books"], "source_records": ["bwb:9781982146160"], "subjects": ["English literature"], "weight": "0.373 ", "full_title": "Frankenstein", "key": "/books/OL35860650M", "works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "covers": [14810195], "identifiers": {}, "classifications": {}, "isbn_13": ["9781982146160"], "lc_classifications": ["PR5397"], "contributors": [{"role": "Introduction", "name": "Stephen King"}], "latest_revision": 7, "revision": 7, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2021-12-26T07:38:26.257011"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2024-08-28T14:01:30.863196"}}, {"works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "title": "Frankenstein: oder Der neue Prometheus", "publishers": ["Coppenrath"], "publish_date": "2023", "key": "/books/OL50534115M", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "identifiers": {}, "covers": [14564456], "isbn_13": ["9783649646099"], "isbn_10": ["3649646099"], "classifications": {}, "contributors": [{"role": "Afterword", "name": "Martin Engelmann"}, {"role": "Translator", "name": "Ana Maria Brock"}], "languages": [{"key": "/languages/ger"}], "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "\u201eH\u00fcte dich, denn ich bin furchtlos und deshalb m\u00e4chtig!\u201c\r\n\r\nNach dem fr\u00fchen Tod seiner Mutter hat Viktor Frankenstein nur ein einziges Ziel: einen Weg zu finden, um den Tod zu besiegen \u2013 egal, was dazu n\u00f6tig ist. Diesen findet er nicht in den mystischen Schriften der Alchemisten des Mittelalters, sondern im Studium der modernen Wissenschaften, und geblendet von der Macht des M\u00f6glichen, ignoriert er Moral und Bedenken. Aber als Viktor aus den sterblichen \u00dcberresten verschiedener Menschen tats\u00e4chlich ein neues Wesen erschafft, ist dies nicht der perfekte Mensch, den er kreieren wollte, sondern ein absto\u00dfendes Zerrbild. Angeekelt flieht Viktor vor dem Gesch\u00f6pf. Allerdings ist das Monster keineswegs gewillt, seinem Erschaffer ein gl\u00fcckliches Leben zu g\u00f6nnen, w\u00e4hrend es selbst in Kummer und Elend lebt. Verbunden durch unvers\u00f6hnbaren Hass, haben die Kreatur und ihr Sch\u00f6pfer nur ein einziges Ziel: den anderen f\u00fcr das Leid zahlen zu lassen, das sie einander zugef\u00fcgt haben \u2026\r\n\r\n10 aufwendig gestaltete Extras versetzen die Leserinnen und Leser in die Zeit des Romans und lassen die Geschichte lebendig werden: eine Karte, Notizbuchseiten, Briefe und vieles mehr! Ein einmaliges Erlebnis f\u00fcr die Fans dieses f\u00fcr das Science-Fiction- und Gothic-Genre wegweisenden Romans."}, "physical_format": "Taschenbuch", "number_of_pages": 272, "latest_revision": 3, "revision": 3, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2024-01-08T09:50:24.056762"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2024-01-08T09:52:13.327288"}}, {"works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "title": "Frankenstein oder Der moderne Prometheus", "publishers": ["Karl M\u00fcller"], "publish_date": "2009", "key": "/books/OL49819414M", "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "identifiers": {"bookbrainz": ["13fab6bd-020f-4e22-a90f-413af32fe36f"]}, "covers": [14534302], "languages": [{"key": "/languages/ger"}], "physical_format": "Hardcover", "translated_from": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "translation_of": "Frankenstein or The Modern Prometheus", "edition_name": "Sonderauflage", "copyright_date": "1981, 2001", "number_of_pages": 293, "isbn_13": ["9783940984791"], "latest_revision": 4, "revision": 4, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2023-10-28T09:17:00.401631"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2026-03-07T17:03:44.184147"}}, {"type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "authors": [{"key": "/authors/OL25342A"}], "isbn_13": ["9798493105944"], "languages": [{"key": "/languages/ger"}], "pagination": "260", "publish_date": "2021", "publishers": ["Independently Published"], "source_records": ["bwb:9798493105944"], "title": "Frankenstein Oder der Moderne Prometheus (illustriert)", "weight": "0.400", "full_title": "Frankenstein Oder der Moderne Prometheus (illustriert)", "works": [{"key": "/works/OL450063W"}], "key": "/books/OL42692049M", "latest_revision": 3, "revision": 3, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2022-12-03T08:01:02.112721"}, "last_modified": {"typ